            <ArticleTitle>Difficult intubation due to undiagnosed congenital tracheal web.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1437-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ijporl.2008.05.021</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Congenital tracheal web is a rare anomaly, usually misdiagnosed as asthma or chronic obstructive lung diseases. Clinical suspicion and appropriate diagnostic imaging combined with endoscopic examinations are the mainstay approach. Symptoms of stridor, dyspnea and recurrent lower airway infections are the most common clinical presentations. We report a case of difficult intubation in a child due to an undiagnosed congenital tracheal web.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
